    "title": "What channel is Thunder vs Celtics on TV tonight? Time, NBA schedule, injury report",
    "text": "Updated March 12, 2026, 6:15 p.m. CTThe OKC Thunder will host the Boston Celtics at 8:30 p.m. CT Thursday.OKC (51-15) outlasted the Denver Nuggets for a 129-126 home win on Monday. It'll now see the return of Chet Holmgren and Alex Caruso, who both missed the Thunder's last two games.Shai Gilgeous-Alexander will also look to make history. He's tied with Wilt Chamberlain for the all-time longest streak of 20-point performances (126 games).Boston (43-22) fell short in a 125-116 road loss to the San Antonio Spurs on Tuesday. Jayson Tatum (right Achilles injury management) has been ruled out.Here's everything you need to know about Thursday's game between the Thunder and Celtics:Order our new book on Thunder's run to NBA title What time is Thunder vs Celtics game tonight?Date: Thursday, March 12Time: 8:30 p.m. CTWhere: Paycom Center in Oklahoma CityWatch Thunder vs Celtics live on FuboWhat channel is OKC Thunder vs Boston Celtics on tonight?TV: FanDuel Sports NetworkStreaming: Prime Video (how to watch)How to watch online: Fubo (free trial)Thunder vs Celtics predictions, picksJustin Martinez: OKC 122, Boston 115Shai Gilgeous-Alexander arguably delivered the best regular-season performance of his career during a win over Denver, and Ajay Mitchell looked as sharp as ever despite missing 20 straight games. Now, the Thunder is getting back two elite defenders in Chet Holmgren and Alex Caruso. OKC is picking up some serious momentum, and I expect it to keep rolling on Thursday with a home win over a Boston team that has Jayson Tatum and Derrick White listed as questionable.Thunder vs Celtics betting oddsOdds via BetMGM as of Thursday, March 12Odds: Thunder by 7.5Over/under: 216.5Moneyline: OKC -300 | Boston +240Thunder vs Celtics injury updatesThunder: Branden Carlson (low back strain) is out. Isaiah Hartenstein (left calf contusion) is out. Thomas Sorber (right ACL surgical recovery) is out. Nikola Topić (G League assignment) is out. Jalen Williams (right hamstring strain) is out.Celtics: Jayson Tatum (right Achilles injury management) is out. John Tonje (G League two-way) is out. Nikola Vucevic (right ring finger fracture) is out. Derrick White (right knee contusion) is questionable.Projected OKC Thunder startersShai Gilgeous-AlexanderCason WallaceIsaiah JoeLu DortChet HolmgrenProjected Boston Celtics startersPayton PritchardDerrick WhiteJaylen BrownBaylor ScheiermanNeemias QuetaJustin Martinez covers the Thunder and NBA for The Oklahoman. Have a story idea for Justin? He can be reached at jmartinez@oklahoman.com or on X/Twitter at @Justintohoops. Sign up for the Thunder Sports Minute newsletter to access more NBA coverage. Support Justin's work and that of other Oklahoman journalists by purchasing a digital subscription today at subscribe.oklahoman.com.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
